A||||10||btoth||code 33!!!  new to me||||4||
Z||000000||btoth||09-15-2001||10:47 AM||||I was driving home from the store yesterday and I noticed that my car didn't seem to be able to make up it's mind between 2nd and 3rd gear.  I looked at my tach and noticed that it was fluctuating up and down (as if the timing was completely off).  It stalled every time I slowed down or stoped till I got it home.  (The car has been running <I>perfectly</I> until now.)  I had heard the muffler backfire once yesterday.  It has done that a few times when the engine is cold, but not when it warms up.  (I do have a bad muffler.)<P>My car:  86 GT; few-month-old refurbished engine; bad muffler (sounds like a free-flow, but it's not); the cat. conv. is less than a year old; I replaced the EGR valve last year and I know it is (was) working; the timing is set as close as it can get to 10 deg.; the plugs are gapped correctly; new MSD coil that improved my idle when I got it.  I can't think of anything else right now.<P>Code 33 = MAP sensor.  My sensor was replaced last year along with most sensors, and I have the steel vacuum lines installed so there should be no leaks.<P>Is it possible that the bad muffler clogged up the inlet pipe and is creating too much back pressure??  Right not the car is pretty much undrivable, I need help!<P>Thanks in advance.||||reg||4
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||09-15-2001||02:23 PM||||If you feel the exhaust is at fault, disconnect it enough to relieve back pressure and see if it will run right. Then try a different MAP sensor.||||reg||1
Z||000002||btoth||09-16-2001||01:21 PM||||*bump*||||reg||1
Z||000003||btoth||09-16-2001||04:52 PM||||Well, it was my coil.  Four month old MSD coil seemed to have gone bad.  I replaced it with my old OEM coil and the car is running fine, and seems to have more acceleration.  The only reason I could see that it would have better acceleration is that the coil must have been slowley dying all this time.||||reg||1
Z||000004||grinthock||09-16-2001||05:38 PM||||I am starting to think that's my problem.  I am going to get a new coil and try it out.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroworldbanner.gif"> </A> <BR>Fieroworld!  Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000005||johnt671||09-17-2001||07:10 PM||||I just posted a thread about an MSD 8226  that was 6 month old failing on my 84 last week.  I just e-mailed MSD about it, and aked if there was anything else I should check.  I went with MSD because a lot of folks said they had trouble with Accels.||||reg||1
Z||000006||btoth||09-17-2001||08:16 PM||||That's what I had done too... and it seemed great until this happened.  Luckily I still have my receipt.  I had ordered it from Summit so I don't think I'll have a problem exchanging it.||||reg||1
Z||000007||NEPTUNE||09-18-2001||09:55 AM||||87 egotrip and I both have Crane Fireball coils. look stock, but have more oomph. Mine is 3 years old. Florida heat hasn't killed it yet! (bought it from summit, cant rememberpart, #). ||||reg||1
Z||000008||btoth||09-21-2001||01:05 PM||||AAARRRRGGGGG!!!!!<P>The problem came back today!!!  What the heck!?  So it's not the coil.  What could it be?  And what could logically make it occur randomly like this.  It was working for the last week and I just drive it down the street and it starts acting up.  Stalled twice... RMPs fluctuating again.||||reg||1
Z||000009||thomas_l||09-21-2001||01:11 PM||||Get a DVOM and check volage drops across all your engine grounds.||||reg||1
Z||000010||btoth||09-25-2001||05:18 PM||||UPDATE:<P>Well, today I was driving back from school, I hadn't had any real problems that last few days.  But as soon as my engine temp reached around 160 all the symptoms came right back instantly! (It occured to me that just driving back and forth to school never gets the engine sufficiantly warmed up and I haven't been just "driving around" much this last month.) So I was assumming that that pointed to something ECM related.  So I went out a spent a bunch of money on a new ACDelco MAP sensor and reset my codes and put my MSD coil back in.  Took my car out for a drive and after an hour or so of 45mph roads everything seemed to settle back to normal and the temp was running around the 200 mark so I'm hoping that I fixed the problem.||||reg||7
